# Feature-branch development workflow

- **Never commit or push directly to `dev` or `main`.**
  - `main` is reserved for production releases (promoted from `dev` via PR).
  - `dev` is the protected integration branch; changes land on `dev` only via Pull Requests from feature branches after CI lint and vulnerability checks pass.
- Before coding, if the current branch is `dev` or `main`, create and switch to a descriptive feature branch off `dev` (`git checkout -b feat/<slug>`, `fix/<slug>`, or `chore/<slug>`).
- Push completed work to `origin/<feature-branch>` (`git push -u origin HEAD`) and open a Pull Request targeting `dev`.
- All Pull Requests must pass the **Lint & Vulnerability Check** (`Frontend (ESLint & pnpm audit)` and `Backend (golangci-lint & govulncheck)`) before merging.
- Do not force-push `dev` or `main`.
